---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
import { appBySlug } from '../../data/apps';

const leaving = appBySlug('marsello')!;
const path = '/alternatives/marsello-alternative';
const title = 'Best Marsello Alternatives for Shopify (2026)';
const desc = 'Evaluate Marsello alternatives using email and loyalty requirements, POS handoffs, matched costs and a migration checklist.';

const altSlugs = ['sequenzy', 'yotpo-email-sms', 'klaviyo', 'omnisend', 'sendlane', 'drip', 'privy', 'firepush'];
const alternatives = altSlugs.map((s) => appBySlug(s)!);

const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Why consider leaving Marsello?",
    "answer": "Consider a change when tested requirements, operator effort or matched costs justify it. Low redemption alone does not establish that loyalty should close."
  },
  {
    "question": "Which option fits a store without loyalty?",
    "answer": "Evaluate email candidates against actual Shopify events, permission controls and operator needs. Sequenzy is a candidate to test, with current integration and commercial terms verified before selection."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can Yotpo Email & SMS replace Marsello?",
    "answer": "No. Yotpo announced full deprecation for December 31, 2025, and its product notice now reports decommissioning. Existing loyalty or reviews requirements need a separate assessment."
  },
  {
    "question": "When should I stay on Marsello?",
    "answer": "Stay when verified online and POS workflows, points controls and operating costs meet requirements. Redemption demonstrates usage; incremental purchases require an appropriate comparison."
  },
  {
    "question": "How should I test lifecycle email?",
    "answer": "Exercise welcome, cart, browse and replenishment requirements with sample profiles. Check event availability, latency, current permission, suppression and purchase exits before enabling sends."
  },
  {
    "question": "How should I migrate?",
    "answer": "Inventory supported data access, identities, consent evidence, suppressions and points obligations. Assign queue owners, test with sending disabled, then drain or retire old queues and deduplicate any authorized replay."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should I keep loyalty and move email?",
    "answer": "A split may fit if loyalty meets requirements and the proposed handoffs are supported. Verify module contracts, event directions and suppression propagation before choosing it."
  },
  {
    "question": "How should I compare costs?",
    "answer": "Use the same eligible audience, sends, channels, locations and time window. Include required modules, reward costs, integration work and staff time; separate recurring expense from one-time migration costs."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm"><a class="link" href="/alternatives">Alternatives</a><span class="mx-2">/</span><span>Marsello alternatives</span></nav>
      <header class="max-w-4xl">
        <p class="catalog-kicker">Email, loyalty and POS decisions</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Best Marsello alternatives for Shopify</h1>
        <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">Start with the workflows the store needs: lifecycle email, online and in-store loyalty, customer identity and staff handoffs. Compare keeping, repairing, splitting or replacing the current setup. An unused module or low redemption rate calls for investigation, not an automatic cancellation.</p>
        <p class="mt-5">The eight original options below are evaluation references in editorial order, not measured performance ranks. Yotpo Email &amp; SMS is retained as a historical route and is no longer an available email replacement.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="mt-12 max-w-4xl">
        <TldrBox title="Shortlist by requirement" picks={[
          { label: 'Email candidate', tool: 'Sequenzy', reason: 'Test the required lifecycle events and current Shopify integration before choosing.' },
          { label: 'Historical option', tool: 'Yotpo Email & SMS', reason: 'Decommissioned; assess any remaining loyalty or reviews needs separately.' },
          { label: 'Catalog exercise', tool: 'Klaviyo', reason: 'Evaluate collection browsing and replenishment with sample profiles.' },
          { label: 'Channel exercise', tool: 'Omnisend', reason: 'Prototype the intended email and SMS journeys and channel permissions.' },
          { label: 'Support scope', tool: 'Sendlane', reason: 'Request a written migration scope and confirm eligibility and fees.' },
        ]} />
      </div>
      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <h2>Current product facts and their limits</h2>
        <p>Marsello documents Shopify POS and ecommerce purchase syncing and configurable points rules tied to payment status. Its default documented purchase reward status is Paid and removal status is Refunded; partial-refund behavior depends on the selected rules. See <a href="https://help.marsello.com/how-do-i-automatically-remove-loyalty-points-for-shopify-orders-marsello-help-center">Marsello’s Shopify points settings</a>. Confirm the store’s actual configuration rather than assuming every refund follows the same path.</p>
        <p>Purchase-point removal and returning points spent on a reward are separate checks. Marsello’s <a href="https://help.marsello.com/en/articles/8138771-how-to-remove-a-discount-code-from-the-sale-in-shopify-pos-staff-training">POS discount-removal instructions</a> describe staff removing the discount and manually returning loyalty points. Test both paths with the retail team.</p>
        <p>Yotpo announced <a href="https://www.yotpo.com/blog/email-sms-migration-partners/">Email and SMS deprecation for December 31, 2025</a>; the <a href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">current lifecycle notice</a> confirms decommissioning. Do not plan an email consolidation onto that retired product. These sources were checked November 25, 2026.</p>
        <h2>Audit loyalty before deciding</h2>
        <p>Measure enrollment cohorts, purchase cycles, issuance, redemption, expiration, reward margin and staff work. Reconcile outstanding balances and customer commitments. Redemption is evidence of usage, not proof of incremental repeat purchasing; use a suitable holdout where feasible. Neither unused points nor attributed flow revenue alone establishes the right stack.</p>
        <h2>Proposed merchant exercises</h2>
        <p><strong>Vinyl drops and mechanical-keyboard group buys:</strong> test launch notices, delayed fulfillment and purchase exits. Compare lifecycle messages with the existing points workflow; no completed migration, revenue gain or lack of customer backlash is claimed.</p>
        <p><strong>Pottery studio and mug shop:</strong> separate workshop-credit obligations from merchandise rewards. Test a student whose class roster email differs from checkout, an online redemption, a POS redemption and a return. Assign identity exceptions to an operator before merging profiles.</p>
        <p><strong>Tea, artisan coffee and tasting-room popups:</strong> model replenishment alongside in-store purchases and QR signup. Record permission by channel and purpose. A tasting-room purchase can end a replenishment sequence only if the proposed integration supplies a usable purchase event.</p>
        <p><strong>Climbing and camping gear:</strong> test collection browsing, variant availability and seasonal offers. Confirm event coverage and incentive conflict rules; do not assume a named provider supplies every event.</p>
        <p><strong>Board games and record-fair booths:</strong> evaluate whether loyalty serves a documented customer need. Compare keeping, changing or retiring it after resolving balances and communications. These are exercises, not merchant results or fixed migration schedules.</p>
        <h2>Authority, ledger and identity checklist</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Name the system of record for online orders, POS orders, loyalty balances, reward definitions and permission evidence. Document supported event directions and latency; no proposed split implies an integration exists.</li>
          <li>Reconcile the points ledger by customer and order: opening balance, earn, redeem, expire, reverse and closing balance. Test paid, cancelled, refunded and partially refunded orders plus removal of an already applied reward. Investigate differences before cutover.</li>
          <li>Map stable customer and order identifiers where available. Queue duplicate emails, changed addresses and shared-household cases for review. Preserve source IDs and avoid merging permission merely because two profiles appear related.</li>
          <li>Confirm supported access or export with each vendor. Inventory available permission timestamps, source, purpose, channel and suppressions; do not assume a member list contains consent evidence or a portable points ledger.</li>
          <li>Test welcome, cart, browse, winback and replenishment with sends disabled. Check permission, suppression and current purchase state at send time, including offline purchases if supported.</li>
          <li>Assign one owner and sender to each points, credit and marketing message. Document conflicts such as workshop-credit notices versus mug winback, and rewards versus seasonal discounts.</li>
          <li>Inventory queued campaigns, delayed automations and retries. Decide which drain and which retire; record the cutoff and reconcile pending work before enabling replacements. Replay only approved events, using stable deduplication keys and current eligibility checks.</li>
          <li>Give retail staff a reward-removal and escalation procedure. Name owners for ledger reconciliation, identity exceptions, permissions, campaigns and rollback. Test the handoff between store staff and ecommerce operations.</li>
          <li>Communicate program changes and unresolved obligations before retirement. Agree a controlled archive and deletion schedule; preserve necessary suppression evidence. Launch only after acceptance checks, with rollback and incident ownership documented.</li>
        </ol>
        <p><strong>Cost comparison:</strong> Use one common time window, eligible audience, sending volume, channels, SMS regions, locations and required workflows. Apply each vendor’s current billable-unit definition and quote. Add required modules, overages, reward costs, integrations and staff time. Show recurring totals separately from one-time mapping, training and migration work. Do not assume Sequenzy uses pay-per-email or that deleting in-store profiles creates a valid saving.</p>
      </article>
      <section class="space-y-12 py-16">
        <p class="catalog-kicker">Conditional options</p>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black">Eight original Marsello alternative references</h2>
        <section class="card prose-shopify" id={alternatives[0].slug}><h3>{alternatives[0].name}</h3>{["Sequenzy is a candidate when the team wants an email-focused workflow. Demonstrate the required Shopify events, identity mapping and purchase exits before selection.", "For vinyl drops and tea replenishment, prototype timing and suppression with sample profiles. Points campaigns should be retained or retired based on the loyalty audit, not an assumption that they never drive redemption.", "Choose if the tested workflow, supported handoffs and current commercial terms meet requirements. No universal lifecycle lead or billing advantage is established here."].map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}<a class="link" href={`/apps/${alternatives[0].slug}`}>Read the app guide</a></section>
        <section class="card prose-shopify" id={alternatives[1].slug}><h3>{alternatives[1].name}</h3>{["Yotpo Email & SMS is decommissioned and cannot serve as the destination for a new Marsello email migration. This original option remains for historical navigation.", "If Yotpo loyalty or reviews is relevant, assess those requirements independently and verify current supported connections to an available email provider.", "Keep email sender selection separate from an assumption that reviews and loyalty require a single suite."].map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}<a class="link" href={`/apps/${alternatives[1].slug}`}>Read the app guide</a></section>
        <section class="card prose-shopify" id={alternatives[2].slug}><h3>{alternatives[2].name}</h3>{["Test Klaviyo against collection browsing, mug replenishment and variant events with sample profiles.", "A hybrid split can fit if the loyalty system and email provider support the required event and suppression handoffs. Assign a data-quality owner.", "Choose after demonstrating those workflows and comparing matched operating costs."].map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}<a class="link" href={`/apps/${alternatives[2].slug}`}>Read the app guide</a></section>
        <section class="card prose-shopify" id={alternatives[3].slug}><h3>{alternatives[3].name}</h3>{["Prototype Omnisend welcome and cart journeys with the intended Shopify events and email or SMS permissions.", "Test delayed events and purchases across the channels the store actually uses.", "Choose if the maintained journeys and operator effort meet requirements."].map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}<a class="link" href={`/apps/${alternatives[3].slug}`}>Read the app guide</a></section>
        <section class="card prose-shopify" id={alternatives[4].slug}><h3>{alternatives[4].name}</h3>{["Ask Sendlane for a written migration scope covering mapping, sender setup and responsibilities. Confirm current support eligibility and fees.", "Demonstrate queue controls and any points-related handoff required by the proposed configuration.", "Choose if the verified scope fits team capacity and the acceptance checks."].map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}<a class="link" href={`/apps/${alternatives[4].slug}`}>Read the app guide</a></section>
        <section class="card prose-shopify" id={alternatives[5].slug}><h3>{alternatives[5].name}</h3>{["For Drip, test tag and product-event branching with current purchase-state exits.", "Preserve permission and suppression evidence; loyalty membership alone does not justify deleting a contact.", "Choose if the tested operator workflow and maintenance costs suit the store."].map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}<a class="link" href={`/apps/${alternatives[5].slug}`}>Read the app guide</a></section>
        <section class="card prose-shopify" id={alternatives[6].slug}><h3>{alternatives[6].name}</h3>{["Evaluate Privy for the capture and messaging tasks the store needs. Test form permission evidence and the supported destination mapping.", "A capture tool can be useful within a wider setup, but the complete email and loyalty requirements still need owners.", "Choose if the demonstrated capture workflow fits; do not assume a Privy-to-Sequenzy connection or a required split."].map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}<a class="link" href={`/apps/${alternatives[6].slug}`}>Read the app guide</a></section>
        <section class="card prose-shopify" id={alternatives[7].slug}><h3>{alternatives[7].name}</h3>{["For Firepush, verify currently supported channels and how identity, permission and suppression connect to the proposed setup.", "A channel addition can fit a specific requirement after testing; it does not automatically replace email or loyalty.", "Use an appropriate holdout to assess incremental margin and include channel and integration work in the common cost comparison."].map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}<a class="link" href={`/apps/${alternatives[7].slug}`}>Read the app guide</a></section>
      </section>
      <article class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl pb-8">
        <h2>Choose a supported operating model</h2>
        <p>A pure ecommerce store may keep Marsello, move email, or retire loyalty after resolving obligations. A hybrid store may benefit from retaining verified POS loyalty while changing email, provided current contracts and integrations support the split. A reviews-heavy store still needs an available email destination. Set milestones from mapping and test results rather than a two-week, four-week or ninety-day promise.</p>
        <p>Monitor duplicate sends, suppression failures, unmatched identities, ledger differences and staff exceptions after launch. Measure attributed revenue separately from incremental margin. Retain or change the setup according to documented requirements and evidence.</p>
        <h2>Related guides</h2>
        <p><a class="link" href="/compare/marsello-vs-klaviyo">Marsello vs Klaviyo</a> · <a class="link" href="/compare/marsello-vs-yotpo-email-sms">Marsello vs Yotpo</a> · <a class="link" href="/alternatives">All alternatives</a></p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Marsello alternatives FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
